---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BOOKING_URL } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
	title="Contact"
	description="Contact Steven Yule at OkArthur about an independent review of a digital or AI investment decision, or about advisory, board, speaking and writing work."
>
	<div class="page-head">
		<h1 class="page-title">Contact</h1>
	</div>

	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			Email <a href="mailto:steven@okarthur.com">steven@okarthur.com</a>, or
			connect on <a
				href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/stevenyule"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a
			>.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you would prefer to talk first, <a
				href={BOOKING_URL}
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer">book a 30-minute call</a
			> at a time that suits you. Booking goes through Calendly, which asks for
			your name and email address.
		</p>

		<h2>If you are considering a <a href="/review/">review</a></h2>
		<p>
			The first call is shorter and more useful if your first message covers a
			few things. Say what the decision is and when it has to be made, and
			which other developments or programmes it touches. Describe what has
			been proposed or delivered by role and not by name, for example the
			main contractor or the platform supplier, and say who has to be
			convinced.
		</p>
		<p>
			After that comes a short call and then a fixed-fee proposal. I take on a
			small number of engagements at a time, and I will tell you on the first
			call whether I can take yours on.
		</p>

		<h2>If you are considering continuing advisory</h2>
		<p>
			Tell me what is being decided or going to market over the coming months,
			and where you need someone independent in the room. Here too, describe
			the people and firms involved by role and not by name.
		</p>

		<h2>Board, speaking and media</h2>
		<p>
			Board approaches and speaking invitations come to the same address. If
			you are writing for the press, mark the message as a press enquiry. The <a
				href="/media/">media page</a
			> has a biography and a photo you can use.
		</p>
	</div>
</Base>
